      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Punk versions from 0.48 before 0.55 for Perl route Extended CONNECT requests to any GET route without an Origin check in ps_serve_one.\n\nOn HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 a WebSocket handshake arrives as an Extended CONNECT, which is matched as a GET and so reaches every GET route, API operation and mount. The Origin check runs only when a websocket route matches. On this transport the handler's status is the handshake response, and a 2xx accepts it.\n\nA cross-origin page can open a WebSocket to any path and learn from its open or error event whether that path returns 2xx.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
